# The three demo folders are written by aescape_course.ipynb.
#
# demo1 costs nothing to regenerate and needs no subscription, and committing it
# would mean the notebook loads a record instead of generating one in front of
# the audience. So it is not committed.
demo1_car_no_agents/

# demo2 and demo3 need a Claude subscription to produce, so one run of each is
# committed as the reference run. Delete a folder to run that demo yourself;
# `git checkout` brings the committed run back.
#
# The reproduction gate's own products are not committed, so that the gate
# really runs on every machine instead of replaying a stored verdict.
demo2_car_one_agent/pipeline_executed.ipynb
demo2_car_one_agent/pipeline_gate.txt
demo3_car_multi_agent/pipeline_executed.ipynb
demo3_car_multi_agent/pipeline_gate.txt
